==English==
[[File:Cupcake Camp Montreal 2009 (4113329873).jpg|thumb|right|alt=A photograph of a cupcake with white frosting and multicoloured sprinkles.|A cupcake.]]

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|cup|cake}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʌpkeɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-cupcake.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small cake baked in a paper container shaped like a cup, often with icing on top.
# {{lb|en|slang}} An attractive young woman.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|first=Thomas|last=Pynchon|title=Against the Day|publisher=Vintage|year_published=2007|page=604|passage=Whatever else this '''cupcake''' might be up to, she was no piker.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[weak]] or [[effeminate]] man.
# {{lb|en|dated}} {{non-gloss definition|Term of endearment}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Kimberly Cates|title=The Perfect Match|passage=“Listen, '''cupcake''',” Cash tried to soothe. “Sometimes when grownups get mad, they say things they don't mean. I'm sure your mother—”}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|small cake}} {{l|en|fairy cake}}
* {{sense|effeminate man}} {{l|en|cockney}}, {{l|en|pansy}}, {{l|en|sissy}}; see also [[Thesaurus:effeminate man]]
* {{sense|attractive young woman}} {{l|en|babe}}, {{l|en|fox}}, {{l|en|stunner}}; see also [[Thesaurus:beautiful woman]]
* {{sense|term of endearment}} {{l|en|cabbage}}, {{l|en|heartmate}}, {{l|en|sweetie}}; see also [[Thesaurus:sweetheart]]

